nazuchem facade and dependency provenance
========================================

The facade is original Nazuchem/ReShiki code, Copyright (c) 2026 Ameyanagi
and ReShiki contributors, licensed MIT OR Apache-2.0. See LICENSE-MIT and
LICENSE-APACHE. The facade calls the separately attributed engines and
kernel; it does not replace their licenses or origins.

Name to structure: nazuchem-n2s is a Rust port of OPSIN by Daniel Lowe,
Copyright 2017 Daniel Lowe, under MIT. The port began at OPSIN 2.9.0,
commit b91b610af5ab07560fedb20730d7aef46bb2bca0, and tracks upstream main
42e87ac6efb1bd9f578986f5ea7ee1faa8e93c91. Complete terms and the port's
notice are in licenses/opsin/LICENSE and licenses/opsin/NOTICE.

Structure to name: nazuchem-s2n began as a port of openclatura 0.4.3,
commit 90dc5bcb4910c196122ec0405d06a32929a8f308, extended in ReShiki.
Copyright (c) 2026 lamalab-org; MIT. It also incorporates OPSIN-derived
registries and a CPython 3.12 integer-set adaptation under Python-2.0.
Complete openclatura and CPython terms, notices and CPython license history
are in licenses/openclatura/ and licenses/cpython/. The engine scope notice
in licenses/nazuchem-s2n/NOTICE qualifies inherited OPSIN generation pins,
the unresolved CPython patch revision, and historical ReShiki source paths.

Molecular perception: nazuchem-kernel adapts RDKit under BSD-3-Clause and
SiMolecule centres under BSD-2-Clause. Complete terms and upstream copyright
notices are in licenses/rdkit/ and licenses/centres/.
licenses/nazuchem-kernel/NOTICE records exact revisions and incorporated
scope. Shared naming vocabulary is original ReShiki code under MIT OR
Apache-2.0; its history is in licenses/nazuchem-ir/NOTICE.

The package expression ANDs the facade's original-code choice with the
established expressions of its engines and kernel:
(MIT OR Apache-2.0) AND MIT AND BSD-3-Clause AND BSD-2-Clause AND Python-2.0.
This applies the dependency terms even when one optional engine is disabled.

nazuchem-s2n's src/data/bluebook/p25_retained.tsv lists the retained heterocycle
names of IUPAC Nomenclature of Organic Chemistry: Recommendations and Preferred
Names 2013, P-25.2.1 Table 2.8, transcribed from
https://iupac.qmul.ac.uk/BlueBook/P2.html; IUPAC holds copyright in the
Recommendations. The names are included as factual data with this attribution;
this package's licences do not cover the file, and no licence is asserted for it
(SPDX NOASSERTION).

Equal-key sorts use Rust's stable sort; no C++ standard library code is included.

Copied notices retain historical paths and broader ReShiki inventories.
The per-file ledger and dependency scope notices identify the incorporated
subset in this standalone repository and preserve the historical source pins.
